# WordPress recipe: permission-normaliser exceptions (slice 6B
# flag 1). Read by the app container's init after its uniform
# pass; format:
#   <octal mode> <path relative to the app-data volume>
# wp-config.php holds the database password (and the session
# salts). The uniform pass would leave it group-shared at 0664;
# the recipe keeps it at 0660 - still writable by the application
# (WordPress runs as the file's owner) and manageable by the
# owner through the owner group, but never readable by other
# accounts on the host.
0660 www/wp-config.php
